        <tr class="hl"><td><b>C &middot; full</b></td><td><b>{{ "%.1f"|format(m.C_full.recall*100) }}%</b></td><td><b>{{ "%.1f"|format(m.C_full.precision*100) }}%</b></td><td><b>{{ "%.0f"|format(m.C_full.clean_doc_rate*100) }}%</b></td></tr>
      </table>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:14px">
        <h3>Reading the numbers</h3>
        <ul><li>Rules alone already catch most <i>structured</i> identifiers &mdash; but leave names in prose, quasi-IDs, signatures and photos.</li>
          <li>The LLM adds context; the VLM adds what is not text at all.</li>
          <li>"Clean page" = zero leaked items &mdash; the metric a compliance officer cares about; the reviewer closes the rest.</li></ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="src">Precision: a redaction box is correct when &ge;30% of its area overlaps ground-truth PII. Reproduce with <span class="mono">python eval/evaluate.py</span>.</div>
